2026-06-05 11:58:44 [deepseek-v4] handle will leak if you later close it in main. A safer approach is to store all threads in a
2026-06-05 11:58:44 [deepseek-v4] vector and join them before `return 0`.
2026-06-05 11:58:44 [deepseek-v4] - If you only need to read the device's response to the boot command, you could read a single
2026-06-05 11:58:44 [deepseek-v4] response and then exit the thread, rather than looping.
