2026-06-05 13:01:22 [nitro@ryzen5] json over serial port as rpc
2026-06-05 13:01:34 [deepseek-v4]  ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.8 ⛲  deepseek-v4 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.047 811.5KB 11.74s
2026-06-05 13:01:34 [deepseek-v4] To use JSON‑RPC over serial instead of raw strings, you can implement a line‑based framing: each
2026-06-05 13:01:34 [deepseek-v4] JSON‑RPC request and response is a single line (terminated by `\n`). The host tool (`echocoms`)
2026-06-05 13:01:34 [deepseek-v4] sends requests and reads complete response lines, then parses them.
2026-06-05 13:01:34 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] Design outline
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] • Framing*
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] - Send: JSON object compacted (no whitespace), followed by `\n`.
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] - Receive: read characters until `\n` (or timeout). Parse as JSON.
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] • Host‑side functions* (add to `tools.h` / `enumports.cpp`)
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] ╭────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │  Function                                      │  Purpose                                                             │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] ├────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │  `rpcSend(comHandle h, utf8 method,            │  Build a JSON‑RPC request object, send it as a line.                 │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │      utf8 params)`                             │                                                                     │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │  `rpcReceive(comHandle h,                      │  Read a line (until newline) with timeout, parse JSON, return result. │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │      utf8 &result, int timeoutMs)`             │                                                                     │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │  `rpcCall(comHandle h, utf8 method,            │  Convenience: `rpcSend` + `rpcReceive` in one call.                  │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] │      utf8 params, utf8 &result, int timeout)`  │                                                                     │
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] ╰────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] • Example call* (replace current `writeComPort` + `readComPort`):
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] comHandle h = openComPort("COM5");
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] utf8 result;
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] int err = rpcCall(h, "reset", "{}", result, 1000);
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] if (err == 0) {
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4]     // result now contains the JSON‑RPC response
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] closeComPort(h);
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] • Pico side (conceptual)* – the firmware should:
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 1. Read lines from CDC (build a buffer until `\n`).
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 2. Parse the JSON‑RPC request.
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 3. Execute the method (e.g., `reset`).
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 4. Send back `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":...,"id":...}` followed by `\n`.
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] Implementation notes for host
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] - Use `SetCommTimeouts` with `ReadIntervalTimeout` for line‑based reading (or implement an explicit
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] line reader that checks for `\n`).
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] - Use `std::ostringstream` to build the JSON string before writing.
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] - Keep a counter for request IDs.
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] If you want, I can provide the three functions (named, no lambda, no arrow) as a drop‑in addition
2026-06-05 13:01:35 [deepseek-v4] to your `tools.h` / `enumports.cpp` pair.
