2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] • Is the intent to…*
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] 1. Replace JSON with a lightweight binary packet for clock sync (e.g., a 1‑byte command +
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] 8‑byte Unix‑microsecond timestamp)? This would be faster to parse on the Pico and reduce overhead.
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] 2. Keep JSON‑RPC but add NTP‑style round‑trip measurement – i.e., include client‑sent
2026-06-05 13:43:27 [deepseek-v4] timestamps and server‑receive timestamps in the request/response, so the host can measure latency
