2026-06-05 14:37:03 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 14:37:03 [deepseek-v4] You can name it anything consistent – `setClock`, `sntp`, `sync` – but "setclock" is a
2026-06-05 14:37:03 [deepseek-v4] clear, self‑documenting choice. If you later merge it with SNTP‑style measurement, you could use
2026-06-05 14:37:04 [deepseek-v4] "sntp" as the method name instead.
