2026-06-05 14:37:24 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 14:37:24 [deepseek-v4] If you meant the system monotonic clock or a software‑based time, there's `time_init()` /
2026-06-05 14:37:24 [deepseek-v4] `time_set()` but `rtc_set_datetime` is the standard way to set a battery‑backed RTC on RP2350.
2026-06-05 14:37:24 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-06-05 14:37:24 [deepseek-v4] For your JSON‑RPC `"setclock"` command, you'd convert the received Unix timestamp into a
2026-06-05 14:37:24 [deepseek-v4] `datetime_t` structure and then call `rtc_set_datetime`.
