2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] Focusing on the new star system for shares as you mentioned.
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] Current star logic (as implemented)
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] From the code:
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - Shares can have a `.stars` string (e.g. `""`, `"★"`, etc.).
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - In `listShare(true)` (the sorted-by-size path used by star command), it displays:
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]   const stars = share.stars || "-";
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - `starCommand`:
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]   - `star` (no args) → calls `listShare(true)` and sets `listCommand = "star"`
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]   - `star <index>` → clears stars on that share
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]   - `star <index> <chars>` → appends the chars to existing stars
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - In `commitShares` (the critical path):
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]   const stars = share.stars || "";
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]   if (roha.config.starshare && (stars.length === 0)) isShared = false;
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - `starshare` config flag (default false) is documented as: "conserve file share by star"
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] So the intended model appears to be:
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - When `starshare` is on, only shares that have a non-empty `.stars` value get committed into the
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] context.
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] - Stars are basically a lightweight include/exclude + priority tag.
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] Observations / potential debug points
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Star accumulation vs. set semantics
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]    The current append behavior (`stars = (share.stars || "") + addStars`) means repeated `star 3
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] ` would give `""`. Is that desired, or should it be a set/replace?
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Clearing logic
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]    `star <index>` with no second token sets `share.stars = ""`.
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]    This is then treated as "no stars" in both display and `commitShares`. Seems intentional, but
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] the display falls back to `"-"` only at list time.
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1] 3. shareList dependency
2026-06-19 13:27:38 [grok-build-0.1]    `starCommand` only works with numeric indices when `shareList` was populated by the last
