2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • Discussion on the starshare behaviour*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] The core issue seems to be a mismatch between what the flag is intended to do and what actually
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] happens at commit time.
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] Intended behaviour (from the flag name and config description)
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] When `starshare` is enabled, the system should be more selective: only shares that have been
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] explicitly marked with stars should have their content loaded into the model context. Unstarred
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] shares should remain in the share list (for visibility and management) but be excluded from the
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] actual payload on `/commit` or `/push`.
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] This is a "conserve tokens" or "explicit opt-in" mechanism.
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] Current flow problems
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] The tracking of "has this share already been committed?" (`rohaSharePaths`) is being mixed with the
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] star decision. Once a share has been seen before, the logic treats it as already "shared", which
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] then overrides the star check in some paths.
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] When a share has no stars, the code is forcing a state that still causes the content to be sent
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] (often because it looks like it needs a refresh or hasn't been marked as shared yet). This makes
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] the star filter ineffective.
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] Key areas worth discussing
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. When should the star filter be evaluated?*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Only at the moment of commit (so the list can still show everything for management)?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Or should unstarred shares be prevented from entering `rohaSharePaths` at all when `starshare` is
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] on?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Should starring a share after it has already been committed trigger an immediate re-commit, or
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] only on the next explicit `/push`?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Separation of concerns*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] Right now there appear to be several overlapping lists:
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - The persistent share metadata (`roha.sharedFiles` / keyed shares)
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - The "currently in context" list (`rohaSharePaths`)
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - The visual list used for commands like `star`
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] It might be cleaner to treat "should this share participate in the current context?" as a derived
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] decision at commit time, rather than mutating the "already shared" tracking based on stars.
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 3. Handling of "modified" shares*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] The existing logic has a strong bias toward re-sending anything that has changed or isn't yet in
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] the active path list. When `starshare` is active, this bias needs to be subordinated to the star
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] check. A share that is modified but unstarred should probably stay out, even if it looks "dirty".
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 4. What does "no stars" actually mean?*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Is an empty star field the same as "never evaluated"?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Should there be an explicit "exclude" state, or is absence of stars sufficient?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Do you want stars to be additive (more stars = higher priority) or just a binary "included / not
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] included" marker?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 5. User workflow implications*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Should `/share` and `/list` (or the star list) behave differently when `starshare` is true?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Should there be a visible indicator in the normal share listing that some shares are currently
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] filtered out due to stars?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - What happens on project load or `/reset`? Should star status survive, or should the flag only
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] affect the current session's commit decisions?
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] • 6. Simpler mental model*
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] One possible direction is to make the star check the first gate at commit time:
2026-06-19 13:47:25 [grok-build-0.1] - If `starshare` is on, only consider shares that have a non-empty stars value.
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] - The "has this been sent before" and "has it changed" logic only applies inside that filtered set.
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] This would keep the management list complete while making the context payload respect the flag.
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like to talk through any of these points in more detail? For example:
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] - How you expect a newly shared file to behave if it has no stars yet
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Whether you want the filter to be "strict" (never send unstarred) or "advisory"
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] - How starring/unstarring should interact with an already-active conversation
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] Happy to explore the trade-offs without jumping to implementation details.
2026-06-19 13:47:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
