2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] • Code review for `json.h`*
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] The parser is functional for basic cases but has several structural and robustness issues. Here's a
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] breakdown:
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] Issues
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 1. String value handling is fragile
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - String parsing always writes into `name`.
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - Value strings only work because the `,` / `]` / `}` handling falls back to `name` when
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] `literal` is empty.
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - This is implicit and easy to break (e.g. with whitespace, empty strings, or certain error
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] paths).
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Unused / incomplete code
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - `parseString()` is defined but never called.
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - The main string parser inside `parseJSON` has its own (partial) unescaping logic.
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - `\uXXXX` handling is just a TODO + `cout`.
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Error handling
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - Errors are reported via `std::cout` and early returns.
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - No structured error information is returned to the caller (just `int` error codes with no
2026-06-19 16:35:12 [grok-build-0.1] meaning documented).
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - The function can leak memory on error paths because objects/arrays on the stacks are not
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] cleaned up.
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Memory management
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - Raw `new`/`delete` with manual ownership transfer.
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - `JSValue` destructor deletes its object/array, but the stacks in `parseJSON` can leave objects
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] behind on parse failure.
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 5. Deprecated / problematic APIs
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - `std::wstring_convert` + `codecvt_utf8` is deprecated since C++17 and removed in some
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] implementations.
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - Global `convert32` instance.
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 6. Other observations
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - No support for `NaN`, `Infinity`, or leading `+` in numbers (follows the "integer vs number"
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] distinction you mentioned).
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - Control character check (`c < 9`) is too aggressive (tabs and newlines are valid whitespace).
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - `toJSON()` does not escape strings properly in all cases (it calls `escape(...)` which isn't
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] defined in this file).
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1]    - `stringMember()` falls back to `toJSON()` for non-string members, which is surprising
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] behavior.
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] Suggested direction
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like me to:
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] - A. Propose a cleaner parser structure (still using the same
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] `JSValue`/`JSObject`/`JSArray` types)?
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] - B. Focus on fixing the current parser with minimal changes?
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] - C. Improve specific parts (string unescaping, error reporting, memory safety, etc.)?
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] - D. Something else (e.g. adding `fromJSON` improvements, better number handling, etc.)?
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-19 16:35:13 [grok-build-0.1] Just tell me which direction you want and how aggressive the changes should be. I won't dump a full
