2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] You're building a PIO-heavy PAL 576i/288p generator on the RP2350 with a multi-stage video
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] pipeline:
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] - `vidbit.pio` → master sync + active-line IRQ
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] - `pixelpump.pio` → feeds two 32-bit "wave trains" (color 0/1 bit patterns)
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] - `onebit.pio` → per-pixel mux between the two trains (using a loopback pin)
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] - `threepin.pio` → drives 3 tristate pins (resistor DAC for Y/Pb/Pr or composite + chroma)
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] - `chroma.pio` / `colortrain.pio` / `pinpump.pio` → color burst + PDM-style chroma
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] - `wst.pio` → teletext insertion
2026-06-20 01:39:59 [grok-build-0.1] 
