2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] Architecture discussion
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] Let’s talk about the relationship between the relay and the bots at a conceptual
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] level.
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Identity & Connection Model
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] Right now the connections are anonymous from the relay’s point of view (just “someone connected on
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 8081”).
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] Questions:
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Should the relay know which bot is which as soon as it connects? (e.g. each bot announces
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] “I am sloppy” on startup)
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Do you want the relay to maintain a registry of active bots with names and capabilities?
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Message Flow Direction
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] There are two main directions:
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] - User → Discord → Bot → Relay
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] - Relay → Bot → Discord
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] Currently it looks like most traffic is being pushed outward from the relay to all bots.
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] Key question:
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] • Where should the decision “should this bot respond?” live?*
2026-06-20 09:54:25 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] Options:
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] ╭──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  Approach                │  Decision lives in  │  Pros                               │  Cons                                       │
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] ├──────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Broadcast + Filter**  │  Each bot           │  Simple relay, bots are autonomous  │  Every bot still has to process everything  │
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Targeted Routing**    │  Relay              │  Less noise on the wire, cleaner    │  Relay needs to understand intent           │
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] │  **Hybrid**              │  Both               │  Flexible                           │  More complex                               │
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] ╰──────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 3. How should users address the bots?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] This feels like the most important UX/architecture question right now.
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] Possible models:
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Explicit addressing — Users @mention a specific bot name in Discord (`@sloppy`, `@riff`,
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] etc.)
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Implicit / system decides — The relay (or a coordinator) chooses which bot should handle
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] a message
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Channel-based — Different Discord channels are assigned to different bots
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Command-based — Users say `/sloppy explain this` or similar
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Always all three, but with roles — They can all see it, but they have different
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] responsibilities
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] Which direction feels right to you?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Bot Differentiation
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] You currently have three named bots. Are they meant to be:
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Distinct personas (different system prompts, different models, different behavior)?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Specialized agents (one is good at code, one at conversation, one at research)?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Mostly interchangeable for now, but you want the ability to make them distinct later?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] This affects whether the relay needs to know about models/personas, or whether each bot process
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] owns its own configuration.
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 5. State & History
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] Should each bot have:
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Its own independent conversation history?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Access to a shared project history (the `relay.md` / project state)?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Both?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] Immediate practical questions
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] To help decide on a direction, I’d like to understand your goals:
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 1. When a user posts a message in Discord right now, what should happen?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1]    - Only one bot replies?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1]    - Any of them can reply?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1]    - They take turns?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1]    - Something else?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Do you want users to be able to deliberately talk to a specific bot (e.g. “I want to
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] talk to sloppy about this”)?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Is the current “all three react to everything” behavior mostly a problem during development, or
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] do you expect it to stay undesirable even in normal use?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 4. How important is it that the bots can talk to each other (bot-to-bot communication)?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 5. Would you rather keep the three bots as fully separate processes, or are you open to the relay
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] having more control over them?
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:26 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-20 09:54:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:54:27 [grok-build-0.1] Take your time. Reply with whichever of these (or other constraints) you want to talk through
