2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] Key implications of this rule
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] This decision pushes us toward a few important architectural choices. Here are the main ones worth
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] deciding on early:
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Where does the @mention filtering happen?
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] This is the biggest near-term decision.
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] • Option A: In the bot (slopbot.ts)*
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - The Discord bot checks if it was mentioned.
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - If not mentioned → it ignores the message entirely (doesn't send it to the relay).
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - If mentioned → it forwards the message to the relay.
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] • Option B: In the relay*
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - Every message still goes to the relay.
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - The relay decides which bot(s) should see it based on mentions, then routes accordingly.
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] • My current lean:* Option A (in the bot) is probably better to start with. It reduces
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] unnecessary traffic and keeps the filtering close to where the mention data already exists cleanly
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] in Discord.
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like to go with that direction for now?
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Commands (`/push`, `/model`, `/share`, etc.)
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] Should commands require an @mention to work, or should they work without one?
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] Examples:
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - Can someone type `/reset` on its own and have it affect the system?
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] - Or must it be `@sloppy /reset`?
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:43 [grok-build-0.1] This affects whether commands are treated as "bot-specific" or "system-wide".
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Non-mention messages
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] What should happen to regular chat messages that don't @mention any bot?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - Completely ignored (even by the relay)?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - Still logged / visible in the relay for history and context?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - Forwarded to the relay but not acted on by any bot?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Bot Identity on Connection
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] Even with @-only behavior, the relay will probably still need to know which bot is
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] connected on each TCP connection.
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] Do you want the bots to announce their identity when they connect (e.g. "I am sloppy")?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 5. Multiple bots mentioned
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] What should happen if someone @mentions two bots in one message?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - Both respond?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - Only the first one?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - None (ambiguous)?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] - Something else?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 6. System / Internal Messages
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] Messages that come from the relay (tool results, status, announcements, etc.) will still
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] need to reach the bots.
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] These should not require an @mention, correct? They need a separate path.
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] Quick questions to clarify direction
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] To help shape the architecture cleanly, a few targeted questions:
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Commands: Should they require an @mention, or work without one?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Plain messages: Should messages with no @mention still reach the relay (for
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] logging/history), or should the bots drop them before they get that far?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 3. Bot identity: Do you want the bots to tell the relay who they are when they connect?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Is the current plan that each bot runs its own model + persona, or will the relay be
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] assigning models to bots?
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 09:56:44 [grok-build-0.1] 5. Any other behaviors you want to explicitly allow without an @mention for now?
