2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] So we're aligning on:
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] - The relay will include a `mentions` field (string array) on messages it sends outward to the
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] bots.
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] - `mentions: []` means "no specific bot is being addressed".
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] - Bots should only act on messages where their name appears in the `mentions` array.
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] This is a clear, simple contract.
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] Current implications with this choice
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:11 [grok-build-0.1] This means we now have two distinct flows to consider:
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 1. User messages coming into the relay (from Discord via a bot)
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - The bot will likely parse the Discord mentions and pass them up.
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - The relay can then decide what to put in `mentions` when it later broadcasts or routes the
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] response.
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 2. Messages going out from the relay (model replies, tool results, status, etc.)
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - The relay will attach the appropriate `mentions` array before sending.
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - A normal model reply to `@sloppy` would probably carry `mentions: ["sloppy"]`.
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]    - Internal / system messages that don't need to trigger a bot response can carry `mentions: []`.
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] A few things worth locking down next
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] Since you've accepted `[]` for no-mentions cases, here are the next natural questions:
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] - Should the `mentions` array be present on every message the relay sends to bots (for
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] consistency), or only sometimes?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] - When the relay generates a model reply, how should it decide what goes in `mentions`?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]   - Just echo back the bots that were mentioned in the original user message?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]   - Or should the relay have its own logic to choose a responsible bot?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] - For messages that originate inside the relay (not triggered by a user message), what should
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] `mentions` usually be?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]   - Always `[]` unless explicitly told otherwise?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1]   - Or do you want some system messages to be able to target a specific bot?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] - On the incoming side: should the bot processes also tag the messages they send to the
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] relay with which bot they are (e.g. `"from": "sloppy"`), so the relay knows the origin?
2026-06-20 10:04:12 [grok-build-0.1] 
