2026-06-21 10:57:45 [nitro@ryzen5] is "rb" faild for second open argument
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1]  ꔀ Relay 1.9.3 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪣  0.7° $0.115 402.8KB 5.09s
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] • No.*
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] `"rb"` is not valid for the second argument to `open()`.
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] Why?
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] - `open()` (the function used in this code) is the low-level file function.
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1]   - Second argument must be an integer (bit flags).
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1]   - Examples: `O_RDONLY`, `O_RDWR`, `O_BINARY`, etc.
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] - `"rb"` is a mode string used only with the higher-level `fopen()`:
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1]   FILE *f = fopen("foo.dat", "rb");   // correct for fopen
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] In `dip.c` you have:
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] gamechn = open(gamfile, RDONLY);     // RDONLY == 0
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] This is using `open()` + `read()` + `lseek()`, not `fopen()`.
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] Correct fix for your Windows build
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] You need to open the file in binary mode. Change the definition or the call.
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] • Best place to fix it* is near the top of `dip.c` or in `dipdefs.h`:
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1] #ifdef _WIN32
2026-06-21 10:58:00 [grok-build-0.1]     #include <fcntl.h>
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1]     #define RDONLY (O_RDONLY | O_BINARY)
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] #else
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1]     #define RDONLY O_RDONLY
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] #endif
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] Or just change the `open()` call in `sysini()`:
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] #ifdef _WIN32
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1]     gamechn = open(gamfile, O_RDONLY | O_BINARY);
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] #else
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1]     gamechn = open(gamfile, RDONLY);
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] #endif
2026-06-21 10:58:01 [grok-build-0.1] 
