2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1]  ꔀ Relay 1.9.3 grok-build-0.1 𝕏 🪣  0.7° $0.060 227.3KB 18.00s
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] • Thanks for sharing the files* (including the updates to the paths, build setup, and the
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] duplicate headers at the end).
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] Glad the gamfile is now loading without crashes. The blank output is a common symptom with this
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] kind of ported 1986-era interpreter.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] Quick diagnosis (no code changes yet)
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Graphics path is the main suspect: All drawing goes through `md_drawblock()` →
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] `altscreen` (the alternate buffer). The only place that should copy it to the real screen is
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] `md_screen_update()`. In the non-UNIX build (`#ifndef HAS_URDATA`) that function is an empty stub,
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] so nothing ever appears.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Text path is also limited: The only `printf`/`putchar` calls are for errors, prompts
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] (save/restore), and the ANSI sequences in `cls()`/`locate()`. The actual game logic only uses a
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] very small subset of opcodes (arithmetic, calls, `OPSHOWI`/`OPSHOWN`/`OPCLEAR`, `OPINPUT`, etc.).
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] There are no print-string, print-char, or status-line opcodes implemented. If the game file
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] is purely graphics-oriented this may be intentional, but it means you will see almost nothing
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] unless the game actually emits `showi`/`clear` calls.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Windows console issues:
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1]   - ANSI escapes (`\033[2J` etc.) are not guaranteed in the classic cmd.exe without extra setup.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1]   - `md_ttyini()` just returns a handle; it does not put the console into raw/non-blocking mode.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1]   - `md_input()` relies on `getchar()` returning 0xFF for "no input", which doesn't happen with the
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] default blocking stdio on Windows.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] - Other notes: The original code was written for an AT&T 7300 (tam.h, urdata ioctl, etc.).
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] The paging, preload, and icon tables look intact, which matches your "loading ok" report.
2026-06-21 11:11:26 [grok-build-0.1] 
