2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] `simonsta` is almost certainly a pure graphics demo (not a text adventure). This DIP
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] interpreter has no text printing opcodes at all — the only things that ever go to the
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] console are errors, save/restore prompts, and the one line in `verify()`.
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] So even if the game is running perfectly, you will normally see nothing on screen unless graphics
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] are being drawn.
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] Quick diagnostic questions
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] While you try a different console, can you tell me:
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 1. Do you see any text at all when it runs?
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1]    (For example: "Unix Interpreter Version A", "Fatal error", save prompts, or even just a blinking
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] cursor?)
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 2. With `_DEBUG` turned on, does it actually hit the debugger?
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1]    i.e. do you ever see the `ZIPDDT>` prompt?
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 3. What console/terminal are you using right now, and what are you switching to?
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 4. Does the process sit completely idle, or does it use CPU?
2026-06-21 11:13:18 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] Things worth checking in the meantime
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] - Try forcing a visible action early. If you can temporarily add a single `printf` inside
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] `op_clear()` or right at the start of `nxtins()`, that will tell us whether the interpreter is
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] actually executing game code.
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] - Some old DIP demos only draw after receiving input. The current `md_input()` on Windows is
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] probably blocking, so the game may be stuck waiting.
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] Let me know the answers to the questions above (especially whether you see the debugger prompt and
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] whether any text appears at all). That will narrow it down quickly.
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] Different console is a good next step — Windows Terminal or ConEmu are usually better than the old
2026-06-21 11:13:19 [grok-build-0.1] cmd.exe for ANSI stuff.
