2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] not used in your build).
2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] Current graphics situation
2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] You’re now getting solid walls of `#` because the current renderer does this:
2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:27 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] bits = 0;
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] for (row = 0; row < GBLEN; row++) bits |= ptr[row * SCRNX2];
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] if (bits != 0) putchar('#'); else putchar(' ');
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] So any block that has even one pixel set becomes a full `#`. Dense graphics (walls, floors,
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] etc.) will look like solid blocks. This is expected with the ultra-simple version.
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] Quick improvement options
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] Would you like me to give you a better version? Here are a few tiers:
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 1. Density-based (easy win)*
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] Use different characters depending on how many pixels are set.
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 2. Sampled pattern (still one char per block)*
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] Pick a few rows and use `+`, `#`, `:`, `.`, etc.
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] 
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] • 3. Better visual (recommended)*
2026-06-21 11:53:28 [grok-build-0.1] Render each 8-byte block using two characters high (e.g. using upper/lower half blocks or
