2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] A couple of issues with the new additions:
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] • 1. `pollMessages()` will hang your loop.* `MsgWaitForMultipleObjects` with `INFINITE`
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] blocks forever until a message arrives. Your main loop will stall there whenever the FIFO has no
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] data.
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] • 2. `MsgWaitForMultipleObjects` only signals that messages exist — it doesn't pump them.*
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] You still need `PeekMessage`/`TranslateMessage`/`DispatchMessage` to actually process them and
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] update the keyboard state that `GetKeyboardState` reads.
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] Here is a corrected `pollMessages()` that uses a zero timeout (non-blocking) and actually pumps the
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] queue:
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] void pollMessages(){
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 	MSG msg;
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 	while(PeekMessage(&msg, NULL, 0, 0, PM_REMOVE)){
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 		TranslateMessage(&msg);
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 		DispatchMessage(&msg);
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 	}
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] }
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] That said, in a console application `GetKeyboardState` may still return stale or empty data because
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] the console window's input is managed by the console subsystem, not your thread's message queue. If
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] you find `anyKeyDown()` always returns false, `GetAsyncKeyState` (which you are already using for
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] escape) is the reliable option — you could scan all 256 keys with it instead:
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] bool anyKeyDown(){
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 	for(int i = 0; i < 256; i++){
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 		if(GetAsyncKeyState(i) & 0x8000) return true;
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 	}
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 	return false;
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] }
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] This polls hardware directly, no message pump required, and you can drop `pollMessages()` entirely.
2026-06-23 09:52:01 [glm-5.2] 
