2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2]  ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 glm-5.2 Z 🪣 0.7° $0.025 74.72KB 9.81s
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] Here's a function that loads the entire file into a `std::vector<uint8_t>` and validates the ELF
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] magic:
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] bool load_elf32(const char* path, std::vector<uint8_t>& buf)
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] {
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	std::ifstream file(path, std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate);
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	if (!file) return false;
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	std::streamsize size = file.tellg();
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	file.seekg(0);
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	buf.resize(size);
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	file.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(buf.data()), size);
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	if (file.gcount() != size) return false;
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	// Validate ELF magic
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	if (buf.size() < 4 || buf[0] != 0x7f || buf[1] != 'E' || buf[2] != 'L' || buf[3] != 'F')
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 		return false;
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 	return true;
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] }
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] Then in `main` you access everything through the buffer:
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] auto* hdr = reinterpret_cast<struct elf32*>(buf.data());
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] auto* phdrs = reinterpret_cast<struct elf32_phdr*>(buf.data() + hdr->e_phoff);
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] auto* shdrs = reinterpret_cast<struct elf32_shdr*>(buf.data() + hdr->e_shoff);
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] - Opens the file once, reads it all in a single pass.
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] - `std::ios::ate` gets the size without a separate stat call.
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] - Returns `false` on any failure — bad open, short read, or bad magic.
2026-06-23 11:45:42 [glm-5.2] 
