2026-06-23 12:25:31 [glm-5.2] • `sh9 entsize:4` — This is likely an array of 4-byte pointers, such as `.init_array` or
2026-06-23 12:25:31 [glm-5.2] `.fini_array` (C++ static constructors/destructors).
2026-06-23 12:25:31 [glm-5.2] • `sh29 entsize:16` — This is almost certainly your `.symtab` (Symbol Table). In
2026-06-23 12:25:31 [glm-5.2] ELF32, each symbol entry (`Elf32_Sym`) is exactly 16 bytes.
2026-06-23 12:25:31 [glm-5.2] • `sh23, sh24, sh28 entsize:1` — These are likely sections that define their granularity as
2026-06-23 12:25:31 [glm-5.2] 1 byte, such as `.ARM.attributes`, `.comment`, or exception index tables.
