2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] strings, just like `readelf` does. Right now, your output says `type:0x1` or `type:0x70000001`.
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] It would be much more readable if it said `type:LOAD` or `type:ARM_EXIDX`.
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] Since you already set up the pattern using `std::map` for `etypes` and `emachines`, we can do the
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] exact same thing for the program headers and section headers.
