2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 3. Flag Decoders
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] Flags are bitmasks, so a map doesn't work as well. A small function that appends characters based
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] on the bits is cleaner.
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] For Program Headers (`p_flags`):
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] std::string pflags_string(uint32_t flags) {
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 	std::string s;
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 	s += (flags & 0x4) ? 'R' : '-';
2026-06-23 13:11:56 [glm-5.2] 	s += (flags & 0x2) ? 'W' : '-';
2026-06-23 13:11:57 [glm-5.2] 	s += (flags & 0x1) ? 'X' : '-';
2026-06-23 13:11:57 [glm-5.2] 	return s;
2026-06-23 13:11:57 [glm-5.2] }
