2026-06-23 13:24:48 [glm-5.2] (Read-Write-Execute). On a desktop OS like Linux or Windows, the loader would aggressively block a
2026-06-23 13:24:48 [glm-5.2] segment from being both Writable and Executable at the same time (to prevent security exploits).
2026-06-23 13:24:48 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-23 13:24:48 [glm-5.2] But because this is bare-metal RP2040 firmware, the linker script just sets all the bits to be
2026-06-23 13:24:48 [glm-5.2] safe. There's no OS memory protection unit active by default, so the CPU doesn't care. It's a neat
2026-06-23 13:24:48 [glm-5.2] detail that proves you're looking at embedded firmware.
