2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] Thank you for sharing these files. I've reviewed all three and have a few observations:
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] • elf32.h*
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] The helper functions `typeString()` and `pflags_string()` are defined (not just declared) in the
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] header without `inline`. This will cause multiple-definition linker errors if the header is
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] included from more than one translation unit. Marking them `inline` or moving the definitions to a
2026-06-24 11:28:13 [glm-5.2] `.cpp` would resolve this.
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] • elfutil.cpp*
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] A potential crash in the section header loop at line:
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] auto shtype = shtypes.find(sh[i].sh_type)->second;
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] If `sh[i].sh_type` is not in the `shtypes` map, `find()` returns `end()` and dereferencing it is
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] undefined behaviour. A safe pattern would be:
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] auto it = shtypes.find(sh[i].sh_type);
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] std::string shtype = (it != shtypes.end()) ? it->second : "UNKNOWN";
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] This mirrors the null-check already done in `emachine_string()` and `typeString()`.
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] • relay.md*
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] The transcript confirms the tool successfully parsed an ARM ELF32 executable with 8 program headers
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] and 32 sections. The documentation of `elf32_phdr` and `elf32_shdr` fields is accurate and serves
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] as useful inline reference.
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] • General design note*
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] The `content` vector stores everything after the ELF header, so every offset access
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] subtracts `sizeof(elf32)`. This works but is a recurring source of off-by-one errors. An
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] alternative would be to store the entire file in `content` and index from offset 0 directly,
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] eliminating the manual subtraction throughout.
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] Everything else looks consistent between the header and implementation. Let me know if you'd like
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] me to elaborate on any of these points or assist with further development.
2026-06-24 11:28:14 [glm-5.2] 
