2026-06-27 13:58:41 [nitro@ryzen5] would an os load binary from elf32? i would like to summarise footprint it required
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] [gpt-5.3-codex] Yes — broadly, an OS (or boot/runtime loader) loads program images from ELF32 using
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] the program headers (`PT_LOAD`), not section headers.
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] For your footprint summary, this is the right mental model:
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Program headers = what gets loaded
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Section headers = mostly linker/debug metadata
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] From your output, loadable segments are:
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x10000000  filesz 0x1560  memsz 0x1560` (flash/code+rodata)
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x20000110  filesz 0x01f0  memsz 0x01f0` (initialized RAM data)
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x10001750  filesz 0x0014  memsz 0x0014` (small flash block)
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x20000300  filesz 0x0000  memsz 0x01fc` (zero-init RAM / bss-like)
2026-06-27 13:58:47 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x200004fc  filesz 0x0000  memsz 0x0800` (heap reserve)
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x20000000  filesz 0x0000  memsz 0x0110` (RAM vector table reserve)
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `LOAD  vaddr 0x20081000  filesz 0x0000  memsz 0x0800` (stack reserve)
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] Quick totals:
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Flash/file-backed bytes loaded = `0x1560 + 0x1f0 + 0x14 = 0x1764` = 5988 B
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Total runtime memory reserved (sum memsz of LOADs)
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	`0x1560 + 0x1f0 + 0x14 + 0x1fc + 0x800 + 0x110 + 0x800 = 0x30f0` = 12,528 B
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Zero-init/reserved only = `0x30f0 - 0x1764 = 0x198c` = 6540 B
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] For embedded (RP2350/pico-style), “OS loader” is often startup/runtime code rather than a full OS
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] kernel, but the ELF loading principle is the same.
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] So yes: summarize footprint from PT_LOAD filesz/memsz and you’ll get the most accurate
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] required image footprint.
2026-06-27 13:58:48 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
