2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] So yes:
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - Use `ph[i].p_offset` as the byte offset in the ELF file.
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - For your current in-memory buffer (file minus ELF header), use:
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] 	- `content_offset = ph[i].p_offset - sizeof(elf32)`
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] And keep bounds checks:
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `ph[i].p_offset >= sizeof(elf32)`
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] - `content_offset + ph[i].p_filesz <= content.size()`
2026-06-27 14:14:04 [gpt-5.3-codex] 
