2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]  ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 gemini-3.5-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.023 7.794KB 12.33s
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] Yes, there are a few ways to achieve sideways U-shapes (and other orientations) depending on
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] whether you want to construct them using multiple box-drawing characters or use single-character
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] symbols.
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] Option 1: Multi-Character Assemblies (Using Box-Drawing Characters)
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] If your maze cells are at least 2x2 in text resolution, you can pair your existing corner
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] characters to create U-shapes facing any of the four cardinal directions.
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] Using the rounded and double-line sets from your specification:
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Open Top (Standard U-Shape)
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Rounded: `╰╯`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Double: `╚╝`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Open Bottom (Inverted U-Shape)
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Rounded: `╭╮`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Double: `╔╗`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Open Right (C-Shape)
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Rounded: Stack `╭` on top of `╰`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Double: Stack `╔` on top of `╚`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Open Left (Inverted C-Shape)
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Rounded: Stack `╮` on top of `╯`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Double: Stack `╗` on top of `╚`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] Option 2: Single-Character Mathematical Operators (Perfect for 1x1 Grids)
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] If each maze cell must be represented by a single character, the Mathematical Operators
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] Unicode block contains a set of square "cup and cap" relations that function perfectly as
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] single-character U-shapes in all four directions:
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊔` (Square Cup / Open Top) — `U+2294`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊓` (Square Cap / Open Bottom) — `U+2293`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊏` (Square Subset / Open Right) — `U+228F`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊐` (Square Superset / Open Left) — `U+2290`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] Option 3: CJK Corner Brackets
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] For a slightly thicker, stylized aesthetic, the Chinese/Japanese/Korean punctuation blocks offer
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] clean, right-angled corner brackets that look like sideways U-shapes:
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `「` and `」` (Left and Right corner brackets) — `U+300C` and `U+300D`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `﹃` and `﹄` (Vertical alternate corner brackets) — `U+FE43` and `U+FE44`
2026-06-27 23:04:00 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
