2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] In the Unicode Mathematical Operators block, the square subset and superset signs are
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] surrounded by several closely related variations. These adjacent characters can be incredibly
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] useful for representing special maze features—such as doors, one-way gates, keys, or start/end
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] points.
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] Here are the characters immediately adjacent to `⊏` and `⊐` in the Unicode table, along with other
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] closely related families:
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 1. The "Equal To" Variants (With Bottom Bars)
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] These characters add a horizontal bar at the bottom, which visually resembles a U-shape with a
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] shelf or a closed threshold.
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊑` (Square Subset or Equal To) — `U+2291` (Open Right with bottom bar)
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊒` (Square Superset or Equal To) — `U+2292` (Open Left with bottom bar)
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 2. Negated Variants (With Slash-Throughs)
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] If you need to represent a locked door, a blocked path, or a wall that cannot be passed, these
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] negated versions of the square subset/superset signs fit the aesthetic perfectly:
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⋢` (Not Square Subset or Equal To) — `U+22E2`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⋣` (Not Square Superset or Equal To) — `U+22E3`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 3. The Rounded Equivalents
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] If you prefer a softer, rounded aesthetic for your maze paths, the standard set theory symbols
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] provide the exact same four orientations in a curved style:
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `∪` (Union / Open Top) — `U+222A`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `∩` (Intersection / Open Bottom) — `U+2229`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊂` (Subset / Open Right) — `U+2282`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊃` (Superset / Open Left) — `U+2283`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 4. Rounded Variants with Bars
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] Just like the square versions, the rounded versions have "equal to" variants with bottom lines:
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊆` (Subset or Equal To / Open Right with bar) — `U+2286`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊇` (Superset or Equal To / Open Left with bar) — `U+2287`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊈` (Not Subset or Equal To) — `U+2288`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] • `⊉` (Not Superset or Equal To) — `U+2289`
2026-06-27 23:06:16 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
