2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] That makes perfect sense. You are referring to iconic, standardized maze layouts that have become
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] part of global culture—designs where, if you saw the blueprint, you would instantly recognize what
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] it is.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] The physical ball-tilt game you mentioned is indeed the classic Brio Labyrinth, and it is
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] one of several legendary designs. Here are the most famous, universally recognized maze designs in
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] the world.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 1. The Classic Tilt Labyrinth (The "Brio" Board)
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] This is the physical wooden game with two knobs to tilt the playfield, a steel marble, and numbered
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] holes from 1 to 60.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] • The Design: It is a highly specific, hand-crafted layout designed to test physical
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] dexterity.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Key Features:
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It features long, straight corridors bordered by dangerous drop-holes.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   The path is linear and numbered, meaning it is technically a single path with obstacles
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] rather than a branching puzzle.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It has highly recognizable "trap zones," such as the winding S-curve near the start and the
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] final, high-pressure straightaway leading to hole 60.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 2. The Cretan Labyrinth (The 7-Circuit Classical Design)
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] This is the oldest known maze design in human history, dating back over 4,000 years. It is
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] associated with the myth of Theseus and the Minotaur.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] • The Design: It is generated using a simple "seed" pattern consisting of a central cross,
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] four corner angles, and four dots. By connecting the endpoints with concentric arches, you always
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] get the exact same iconic shape.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Key Features:
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It is strictly unicursal (one continuous, non-branching path to the center).
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It has seven concentric pathways (circuits).
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It has a distinct, symmetrical "brain-like" appearance.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 3. The Pac-Man Maze (Arcade Board)
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] Designed by Toru Iwatani in 1980, this is arguably the most viewed and played maze layout in human
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] history.
2026-06-27 23:14:21 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] • The Design: A highly functional, symmetrical grid designed specifically for gameplay
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] balance, line-of-sight, and escape routes.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Key Features:
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   The Ghost House: A central, rectangular enclosure where enemies spawn.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   Warp Tunnels: Openings on the far left and right edges that wrap around to the
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] opposite side.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   The Symmetry: The left half is a perfect mirror image of the right half.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   The Safe Zones: Specific T-junctions designed to let the player outmaneuver
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] pursuers.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 4. The Chartres Labyrinth (The Medieval Christian Design)
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] Inlaid into the stone floor of Chartres Cathedral in France around 1200 AD, this design has been
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] copied in parks, gardens, and churches worldwide.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] • The Design: A highly complex, circular, 11-circuit design divided into four quadrants.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Key Features:
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   A central, six-petaled flower shape (the "Rosette").
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   A jagged, decorative outer border called the "lunette" that looks like half-circles or
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] teeth.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   The path winds through all four quadrants, taking the walker close to the center, then far
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] away, before finally leading to the middle.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 5. The Hampton Court Palace Maze
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] Planted in the UK around 1690, this is the archetypal "hedge maze" layout that popularized the
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] concept of branching paths and dead ends in modern culture.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] • The Design: A trapezoidal (keystone) shape rather than a perfect square, designed to fit
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] a specific corner of the palace gardens.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] • Key Features:
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It is a multicursal maze (many branches and dead ends).
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It features two distinct halves wrapped around a central goal containing two trees.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash]     *   It is famous for being the subject of the "always turn left" (or right) wall-following
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] myth, which actually does not work perfectly here because some loops isolate the center.
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] Quick Comparison of Iconic Designs
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] 
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] ╭──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────╮
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] │  Name of Design              │  Visual Shape                │  Defining Characteristic        │
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] ├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] │  **Brio Labyrinth**          │  Rectangular Grid            │  Numbered path with 60 holes    │
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] │  **Cretan Labyrinth**        │  Circular / Rounded Cross    │  7-circuit, unicursal classic   │
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] │  **Pac-Man Board**           │  Tall Blue/Black Rectangle   │  Symmetrical, central ghost box │
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] │  **Chartres Labyrinth**      │  Four-Quadrant Circle        │  11-circuit, central rosette    │
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] │  **Hampton Court**           │  Trapezoid                   │  Classic branching hedge paths  │
2026-06-27 23:14:22 [gemini-3.5-flash] ╰──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────╯
