im/total view might collapse to just vendor name + credit, or add a sum row at the bottom. Something like:```total: $-9.9234 across 8 vendors, 214 models```Or maybe flag which accounts are critically low and need topup.Want to tackle the scan command first, or the account UI trim?User: after a scan, not trim, available is the word i should have usedKimi: Got it - after a scan, not trim. **Available** is the right word. So the account command should show what's actually available right now, post-scan. Filter out the models that are broken, rate-limited, or out of credit.Something like:```> /account availabledeepseek: 2/2 models available, $-3.48 creditzai: 6/8 models available, $-5.38 creditmoonshot: 10/12 models available, $-2.16 credit...```Or just a clean list of which vendors have working endpoints and how many models you can actually reach. The scan feeds the account view with real availability data.User: nice, i like the data no table mode, what mode could that be called?Kimi: "List mode" or "compact mode" - but since you like "data no table," maybe:- **Raw mode**- **Plain mode**- **Stream mode**- **Tsv mode** (if it's tab-separated)- **Bare mode**- **Naked mode** (no formatting)- **Log mode**Or if you want something more distinctive: **spool mode**, **scroll mode**, **terminal mode**, **flat mode**, **unadorned mode**.My pick: **raw mode** or **plain mode**. Clear, unambiguous, contrasts with the table UI.User: > >/config0 squash : squash message sequences in output : false1 reasonoutloud : echo chain of thought : false2 tools : enable model tool interface : false3 search : enable search tool interface : true4 commitonstart : commit shared files on start : false5 saveonexit :  save conversation history on exit : true6 ansi : markdown ANSI rendering : true7 verbose : emit debug information : false8 broken : ansi background blocks : false9 logging : log all output to file : true10 debugging : emit diagnostics : false11 pushonshare : emit a /push after any /share : false12 slopprompt : rawmode stdin with shortcode support : true13 resetcounters : factory reset counters and files on reset : false14 returntopush : hit return to /push - under test : false15 slow : experimental output at reading speed : false16 slops : console worker scripts : false17 budget : cheap models for the win : false18 syncRelay : one thing at a time mode : true19 listen : listen for remote connections on port 8081 : true20 project : load current project on start : true21 thinking : enable thinking mode with dual purpose models : true22 underline : enable underline markdown support : false23 persona : extend system prompt : true24 starshare : conserve file share by star : trueKimi: I see - your `/config` list with 25 toggles. Some interesting ones:- **rawmode stdin with shortcode support** (`slopprompt: true`) - this is probably close to what you were looking for as a "data no table" display mode- **squash message sequences** (`squash: false`) - collapse repeated messages- **thinking mode** (`thinking: true`) - dual purpose models, probably for reasoning models- **budget** (`budget: false`) - cheap models for the win, disabled- **syncRelay** (`syncRelay: true`) - one thing at a time, serial processing- **listen** (`listen: true`) - remote connections on 8081The `slopprompt` flag at #12 sounds like it might already be a raw/plain mode for prompts. But for output display, you don't have a dedicated "no table" mode yet.Maybe add a config toggle:```25 rawout : disable table formatting in output : false```Or repurpose `slopprompt` to also affect output, though that might be confusing.What does `slopprompt` actually do right now - just stdin parsing, or does it affect display too?User: can i share this chat?Kimi: Yes, you can share this chat. Kimi has a share feature - look for a share button in the interface, or you can use the `/share` command if your client supports it.From your config list, `pushonshare` is set to `false` (item 11), so sharing won't auto-push to your relay. And `starshare` is `true` (item 24), which conserves file share by star - probably means starred conversations get shared more efficiently or with less overhead.If you want to share, just hit the share button or say `/share` and you'll get a link. The conversation will be viewable by anyone with the link.Want me to do anything specific before you share - like summarizing the model sphere todo list we built up?
