2026-06-29 14:13:15 [deepseek-v4-flash] I see the code and output. The main problem is that `clampSample33` returns `0` for out-of-bounds
2026-06-29 14:13:15 [deepseek-v4-flash] cells, but `boxIndex` expects `"▢"` (codepoint 9634) for empty cells. This causes a mismatch at the
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] edges and inner corners, producing many `"*"` characters as fallback.
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] Additionally, `boxIndex` only handles a few specific 3×3 patterns (corners and straight lines), but
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] the actual maze shapes include Tees, crosses, etc. The function `getEdge` already computes the
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] correct edge type from the four cardinal neighbors, but it is never called – `outlineGrid` uses
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] `boxIndex` instead. This suggest the design is unfinished.
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] Here are concrete observations and suggestions:
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 1. Fix `clampSample33` – replace `0` with `9634` (`"▢".codePointAt(0)`) for out-of-bounds
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] cells, or better, use the original space character `32` if the grid is not a pure block grid. Since
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] the grid after `blockHashGrid` only contains `"▢"` and `"▣"`, use 9634 for empty.
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 2. Use `getEdge` instead of `boxIndex` – it correctly identifies all 11 edge shapes from
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] the four cardinal neighbors (`u,d,l,r`). The comment "if 3x3 has single solid corner then use
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] Corner" seems to hint that this is the intended approach.
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 3. Edge detection – `getEdge` works on the 4-connected neighbors of the centre cell. To use
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] it, you only need the four cardinal values (up, down, left, right) from the 3×3 sample. For
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] clarity, you could extract them inside `outlineGrid` instead of building the full 3×3 array.
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 4. Wrapping vs clamping – The current code uses `wrapSample33` for the outline step. That
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] is fine if the maze is assumed to be periodic, but the outer border of your maze is solid walls. If
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] you want rounded corners on the outer boundary, you must use `clampSample33` (with the corrected
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] empty value) so that outside cells are treated as empty, not wrapped.
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] 5. The `"*"` characters – They appear where `boxIndex` returns -1. After fixing the above,
2026-06-29 14:13:16 [deepseek-v4-flash] they should become proper box‑drawing characters.
