2026-06-30 15:36:13 [deepseek-v4-flash]  ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 deepseek-v4-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.004 45.94KB 5.17s
2026-06-30 15:36:13 [deepseek-v4-flash] The ANSI escape sequence to clear from the current cursor position to the end of the line is:
2026-06-30 15:36:13 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] \x1b[K
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `\x1b` is the ESC character (hex 1B).
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] - `[K` is the CSI (Control Sequence Introducer) command for "Erase in Line" with parameter `0`
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] (default – clear to end of line).
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] - You can also use `\x1b[0K` explicitly; `0` is the default.
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] To clear the entire line (cursor stays), use `\x1b[2K`.
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] To clear from cursor to beginning of line, use `\x1b[1K`.
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] In your `traffic.ts`, you could combine it with cursor up and carriage return to redraw the lane
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] cleanly. For example:
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] Deno.stdout.write(encoder.encode("\x1b[A\x1b[K")); // cursor up, then clear line
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] console.log(lane, pump);
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] This avoids leftover characters when the lane string changes length.
2026-06-30 15:36:14 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
