2026-06-30 15:45:41 [nitro@ryzen5] i want fadepumps to snapshot fade and return previous values, it is win32 tradition
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]  ꔀ Relay 1.9.4 deepseek-v4-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.006 62.57KB 7.32s
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] Yes, that fits the "snapshot return" pattern used in Win32 APIs like `SetCursorPos` (returns
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] previous position) or `SetTimer` (returns previous timer ID).
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] Here's the updated `fadePumps`:
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] function fadePumps(): number[] {
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]     const previous = [...pump];   // snapshot current values
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]     for (let index = 0; index < pump.length; index++) {
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]         let integral = pump[index] | 0;
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]         const fade = integral >> 2;
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]         pump[index] = fade ? integral - fade : 0;
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]     }
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash]     return previous;   // return the values before fading
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] - The snapshot is taken before mutation.
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] - The fade is applied in place to `pump`.
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] - The caller gets back the previous values, which can be used for something like logging, undo, or
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] differential tracking.
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] Usage remains the same – a plain call `fadePumps()` still works, but now you can also do:
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] const prevPump = fadePumps();
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] console.log("faded from", prevPump);
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] If you want to keep the original function name but also offer a non‑mutating version, you could
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] create a separate `computeFade` pure function, but the above keeps it simple and follows the Win32
2026-06-30 15:45:49 [deepseek-v4-flash] convention.
