2026-06-30 17:44:44 [deepseek-v4-flash] You're right – I misunderstood your indexing. I apologize.
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] Looking at your `gridWindow` more carefully:
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] let offset = (wy + y * 2) * span + ((wx + x) >> 2);
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] let shift = ((wx + x) & 3) << 1;
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] let bit01 = (src[offset] >> shift) & 3;
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] let bit23 = (src[offset + span] >> shift) & 3;
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] let index = (bit23 << 2) | bit01;
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] You treat each source byte as four 2‑bit values (two bit pairs per byte row). The quad character
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] then maps the upper 2‑bit value from the row `y2` to the low nibble of the index, and
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] the lower 2‑bit value from the next row (`y2+1`) to the high nibble. That gives a 4‑bit
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] index where the two bits from each row represent two horizontally adjacent pixels (or a 2‑level
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] intensity).
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] This is a valid design – it allows a 2‑bit‑per‑pixel grayscale (4 levels) encoded in the `quads`
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] array. The `quads` array you provided (`" ▘▝▀▖▌▞▛▗▚▐▜▄▙▟█"`) actually matches the 2×2 quadrant
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] pattern, but you're using it to represent 2‑bit combinations (not 1‑bit quadrants). That's clever –
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] each quad character here corresponds to a 2‑bit row pair, not the classic four‑corner bits.
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] So your code is consistent with that approach, and my earlier "fix" would have broken that design.
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] Thank you for correcting me.
2026-06-30 17:44:45 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
