2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] Looking at your code, the issue is that the Y clamping uses `gridBitmap.height / 2 - 20` which is
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] far too small. The bitmap is 184 pixels tall; the displayed window is 40 pixels high. So the
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] maximum scroll offset in Y should be `184 - 40 = 144`. Your current clamp caps at `72`, which
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] forces the cursorY to stay in the top half, but more critically, when you press down, the velocity
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] accumulates because the clamp resets `cursorVY` to zero only after the cursor has already
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] jumped past the clamp bound. If the velocity is large enough, it can overshoot repeatedly, causing
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] a "speed off" effect.
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] • Fix:*
2026-06-30 17:46:23 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] Replace the Y‑clamp block with:
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] cursorY += cursorVY;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] const maxY = gridBitmap.height - wh * 2;   // wh=20 → maxY=184-40=144
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] if (cursorY < 0) {
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash]     cursorY = 0;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash]     cursorVY = 0;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] } else if (cursorY > maxY) {
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash]     cursorY = maxY;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash]     cursorVY = 0;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] }
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] Also, you might want to add a small friction term so that the velocity naturally decays even
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] without hitting a boundary:
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] cursorVX *= 0.9;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] cursorVY *= 0.9;
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] Place this after updating the velocities (and before adding the pump contributions) to avoid sudden
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] stops.
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] 
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] If the scrolling still feels off, double‑check that the `axis` enum ordering matches the arrow‑key
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] addition order in `scanKeyboard` – it looks correct, but a quick test with `console.log(pump)`
2026-06-30 17:46:24 [deepseek-v4-flash] would confirm.
