2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] In the context of Unicode and UI design, it is almost universally referred to as the "Hamburger
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] icon" (U+2630 ☰, "Trigram for Heaven").
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] However, for a "sandwich" specifically, there isn't a single standardized Unicode character that
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] looks like the three-line UI element. People often use these:
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • ☰ (U+2630): The standard "Hamburger" (Trigram for Heaven).
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • ≡ (U+2261): "Identical to" (often used as a cleaner, tighter Hamburger).
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • 🔣 (U+1F523): Input symbols (sometimes used as a menu/sandwich placeholder).
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • 🥪 (U+1F96A): The literal Sandwich emoji (rarely used for UI, but accurate to the name).
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • For a technical project like `biblispec`:*
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] If you want to maintain your "living document of linguistic latitude," using ☰ is the
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] industry standard for menus. If you want to lean into your specific theme of "specifications,"
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] ≡ is often preferred by developers for its mathematical precision (representing
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] identity/equivalence).
2026-07-01 08:47:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
