2026-07-01 08:49:20 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] By using `1006`, the terminal will report coordinates as `\x1b[<button;x;yM` (for click down) and
2026-07-01 08:49:20 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] `\x1b[<button;x;ym` (for release). This is significantly easier to parse than the older "X10" mode
2026-07-01 08:49:20 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] because it handles coordinates larger than 223 and provides the button state clearly.
