2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 2. The Required "Off" Switch
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] As mentioned before, if your program crashes or exits without sending the "off" sequence, the
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] user's terminal will stay in mouse-tracking mode (where clicks don't highlight text). You should
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] include this in your `stopRunning` or a `finally` block:
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] const mouseOff = "\x1b[?1006l";
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] export function stopRunning() {
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]     Deno.stdout.write(new TextEncoder().encode(mouseOff)); // Clean up
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]     Deno.stdin.setRaw(false);
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]     running = false;
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
