2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 3. A Note on Parsing
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Because you are using `keyboardTask` with a buffer, be aware that mouse events can arrive in the
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] same buffer as keyboard events.
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] If a user clicks, the buffer will contain the full sequence `\x1b[<0;10;5M`. Your `keyboardTask`
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] logic will need to check if the buffer starts with `\x1b[<` to decide whether to treat it as a
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] mouse event or a keyboard key.
2026-07-01 08:56:56 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
