2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Why this works:
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • `.slice(-n)`: When you provide a negative number, JavaScript counts back from the end of
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] the array.
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • Safety: If the array has fewer than 3 items (e.g., `["a", "b"]`), `.slice(-3)` will
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] simply return all available items (`["a", "b"]`) without throwing an error.
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • Immutability: This creates a new array and does not modify your original list.
2026-07-01 09:02:55 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
