2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] if (!isNaN(index)) {
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]     // It is a valid number, proceed...
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] • Note:* Always check `isNaN()` after `parseInt()` if you aren't sure the user typed a
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] valid number, otherwise you might end up with `NaN` (which is technically a "number" in JS, but
2026-07-01 09:47:27 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] will break your array index lookup).
