2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Beyond moving the cursor and toggling blink, you can manipulate its appearance (shape) and state
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] (visibility) using further ANSI escape sequences.
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Here are the reusable functions to control the cursor's shape and visibility:
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 1. Changing Cursor Shape
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Many modern terminals allow you to change the cursor from a block to a bar or underline. This is
2026-07-01 13:02:48 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] often used to provide feedback on different input modes (e.g., Insert vs. Overwrite).
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] /**
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * Sets the cursor shape.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 0: Blinking Block (default)
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 1: Blinking Block
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 2: Steady Block
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 3: Blinking Underline
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 4: Steady Underline
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 5: Blinking Bar
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * 6: Steady Bar
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  */
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] function setCursorShape(shape: number): void {
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	const escapeCode = `\x1b[${shape} q`;
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	Deno.stdout.writeSync(new TextEncoder().encode(escapeCode));
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] // Example: Change to a steady bar
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] setCursorShape(6);
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 2. Controlling Visibility
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] If you are rendering a custom TUI (Text User Interface) or an animation, you often want to hide the
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] cursor to prevent it from flickering over your content.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] /**
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * Hides the terminal cursor.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  */
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] function hideCursor(): void {
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	const escapeCode = "\x1b[?25l";
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	Deno.stdout.writeSync(new TextEncoder().encode(escapeCode));
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] /**
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * Shows the terminal cursor.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  */
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] function showCursor(): void {
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	const escapeCode = "\x1b[?25h";
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	Deno.stdout.writeSync(new TextEncoder().encode(escapeCode));
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 3. Saving and Restoring Position
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] If you need to move the cursor to perform an action (like printing a status message at the top of
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] the screen) and then return to the user's previous typing location, use the save/restore codes.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] /**
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * Saves the current cursor position.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  */
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] function saveCursorPosition(): void {
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	const escapeCode = "\x1b[s";
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	Deno.stdout.writeSync(new TextEncoder().encode(escapeCode));
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] /**
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  * Restores the saved cursor position.
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite]  */
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] function restoreCursorPosition(): void {
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	const escapeCode = "\x1b[u";
2026-07-01 13:02:49 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 	Deno.stdout.writeSync(new TextEncoder().encode(escapeCode));
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] }
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Summary Table of ANSI Sequences
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] ╭────────────────────────┬────────────────╮
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  Action                │  Sequence      │
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] ├────────────────────────┼────────────────┤
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  :---                  │  :---          │
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  **Hide Cursor**       │  `\x1b[?25l`   │
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  **Show Cursor**       │  `\x1b[?25h`   │
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  **Save Position**     │  `\x1b[s`      │
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  **Restore Position**  │  `\x1b[u`      │
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] │  **Set Shape**         │  `\x1b[<N> q`  │
