2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] 
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] Pro-Tip for Deno
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] When using these in production, ensure your program handles the `SIGINT` (Ctrl+C) signal. If your
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] program exits while the cursor is hidden, the user's terminal will remain without a cursor until
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] they restart it. You can use `Deno.addSignalListener("SIGINT", () => { showCursor(); Deno.exit();
2026-07-01 13:02:50 [gemini-3.1-flash-lite] });` to ensure the cursor is restored on exit.
